      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T16:08:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As an alternative to this, wdyt about SkPathConvexity and SkFirstPathDirection just being std::optional\u003cSkConvexity\u003e and std::optional\u003cSkPathDirection\u003e?\n\nI suppose there\u0027s no SkConvexity right now because we just return a bool, but that seems like a good improvement too. Most of the annoyance I have with these types in general is the overlap between SkPathDirection and SkFirstPathDirection, and std::optional\u003cSkPathDirection\u003e fully captures the intent of SkFirstPathDirection.\n\nIt also makes the need for SkOppositePathDirection irrelevant, since CW vs. CCW are trivial to do inline, and you ever flip them if you actually have a direction to flip.\n\nIf we defined SkConvexity, it could go into the `include/core/SkPathTypes.h` header as well, and then we\u0027d not need to introduce a new private header for SkPathEnums.\n\nIt\u0027s more involved changes for sure, but WDYT? Maybe we CC the Brian\u0027s to get their thoughts too?",
      "revId": "92a65d3ae9268e1d5766f91753b66329c7d3682d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
